  "enhanced_information": "The drug prescribed by the fertility specialist is likely a selective estrogen receptor modulator (SERM), which can stimulate receptors in low hormone environments and inhibit them in high hormone environments. SERMs are known to be associated with certain adverse events, including deep venous thrombosis (DVT), which is a common risk due to their estrogenic activity. While hirsutism can occur due to increased estrogenic activity, it is not a primary adverse event associated with SERMs. Osteoporosis is not typically linked to SERMs but rather to long-term estrogen deficiency. Thrombophilia is more related to genetic factors and not directly caused by SERMs. Visual disturbances are less common and not a primary concern with SERMs. Therefore, the most likely adverse event associated with the drug prescribed is deep venous thrombosis.",
